# Rust build output (compilation artifacts)
/target

# Cargo lockfile override (keep Cargo.lock for binary projects, but ignore if needed)
# For binary apps like shortcut-sheet, Cargo.lock IS usually committed, but /target must be ignored.

# IDE / Editor configuration folders
.vscode/
.idea/
*.rs.bk

# OS-generated files
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Temporary log files
*.log

/target/
replica/tmp/
**/*.rs.bk

# The target app, left on disk and never committed.
#
# replica/package/ is the vendor's own extracted MSIX: signed binaries, their tile art and
# their manifest. Nothing in it is ours to redistribute, and the clean-room rule in
# replica/recon.md says the same - it is read for metadata, not shipped.
# replica/appdata/ is this machine's copy of the app's settings and progress, with registry
# hives in it that name the user.
# demo.mp4 is 371 MB, which is past what GitHub will accept in a push at all.
replica/package/
replica/appdata/
replica/screens/demo.mp4
*.mp4